  "id": "scat",
  "term": "SCAT",
  "definition": "In this source, scat is an evidence-type category used to label mammal observations in citizen-science data rather than a sighting of the animal itself. It refers to observations based on this kind of animal sign and can be used to help describe how the observation was obtained.",
